{
  "$comment": "Fingerprints of every sample in test-output/samples/ (each sample run by scripts/generate-samples.ts in its own process with the creation instant pinned, in UTC). Regenerate deliberately with `npx tsx scripts/verify-samples.ts --update`, and say why in the release notes: a changed hash means existing output changed. Mode `bytes` is a SHA-256 of the file; mode `semantic` is a SHA-256 of a canonical projection of the document, reserved for encrypted samples (CSPRNG file key and IVs), of which this repository has none. Each entry's `since` names the release whose output the hash is: it is carried forward untouched while the sample is unchanged, and moves to the release doing the rebaseline when the hash changes, so the chain 1.3.0 -> 1.4.0 -> … stays auditable and every re-anchoring is visible in the diff.",
  "baselineVersion": "1.4.0",
  "provenance": "Chain origin: pdfnative-react 1.3.0 on pdfnative 1.8.0 — the first release with a pinned creation instant (creationDate / setDefaultCreationDate) and UTC dates, so every entry was anchored at 1.3.0 with no earlier reference to inherit. Captured on Windows 11 (Node 22) by running scripts/generate-samples.ts twice in a row under TZ=UTC, then held by the Linux, Windows and macOS runners of sample-regression.yml. The two-time-zone proof (Pacific/Kiritimati vs America/Los_Angeles, over dist/index.js) is tests/regression/reproducible-build.test.ts. fonts/fonts-prop.pdf and fonts/fonts-prop-sync.pdf are one document rendered through both entry points and are identical by design (IDENTICAL_SAMPLE_GROUPS). Re-anchored at 1.4.0 on pdfnative 1.9.0 (release-notes/v1.4.0.md, Upgrade section): every sample that embeds a font moves through the engine ledger — lean, compact subsets with a six-letter subset tag (C6, C21, C28), one text object per line (C25), /ActualText spans on right-to-left and reordered runs (C20, C27) — and shrinks by a factor of three to nine (fonts/fonts-prop*, layout/page-setup, layout/print-pdfx4, layout/watermark-header-footer, text/math, text/typography-engine, text/typography-french); layout/cmyk.pdf gains the page transparency group the engine now writes for a translucent watermark (C11, +53 bytes); charts/charts-v2.pdf gains a per-value-colour chart and an unlabelled series (sample edit); fonts/scripts-27.pdf is renamed fonts/scripts-32.pdf and extended with the five Indic scripts of 1.9.0; five samples are new (text/rtl-direction, media/image-jpx, layout/print-spot-colours, layout/print-dual-pdfa2b-pdfx4, fonts/scripts-32). The 27 base-14-only samples (invoice, report, structure/*, forms/*, charts/charts, agent/*, quality/*, media/*, table/*, text/typography, text/nested-lists, layout/*) keep their 1.3.0 hashes untouched: engine 1.9.0 is byte-identical for documents that embed no font and carry no right-to-left or shaped text.",
  "creationDate": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "timezone": "UTC",
